# Only generated artefacts are ignored. Every source file needed to inspect,
# modify and build the client is tracked:
#
#   fwu/*.py         the client library and CLI
#   tests/*.py       the test suite
#   research/*.py    analysis tooling that regenerates the protocol findings
#   pyproject.toml   packaging and the fwu-info entry point
#   Makefile         build, install, test and lint targets
#   LICENSE README.md research/*.md
#
# The client has no third-party dependencies, so a clone plus a Python 3.9+
# interpreter is a complete build environment.

# Python bytecode
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo

# Build and packaging output
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/

# Virtual environments
.venv/
venv/

# Test and lint caches
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage

# Intel-distributed binaries and firmware payloads. These are inputs to the
# analysis, not inputs to the build - nothing here is needed to compile, test
# or run the client. research/INPUTS.md records their hashes so an analyst can
# verify their own copies, and research/analyze_pe.py regenerates every
# finding from them.
*.bin
*.exe
*.CAP
*.zip
